{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And let approach.</b> Do not wonder because it first said, \"Go up to YHWH,\" and afterward, \"and let Moses approach alone,\" and it did not say ונגשת (\"and you shall approach\"), for such is the way of the language: \"And YHWH rained upon Sodom and upon Gomorrah brimstone and fire from YHWH out of heaven\" (Genesis 19:24) — the meaning is, from Him. And Samuel said: \"And YHWH sent Jerubbaal and Bedan and Jephthah and Samuel\" (1 Samuel 12:11), and did not say ואותי (\"and me\"). And there are many like this."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:53.007640596Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}